.TH HOWDY-GTK 1 "November 2026" "howdy 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
howdy-gtk \- graphical user interface for Howdy face authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B howdy-gtk
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B howdy-gtk
is the GTK interface used to set up and manage
.BR howdy (8):
it registers and removes face models for user accounts, previews the
infrared camera feed and runs the first-run onboarding wizard which
downloads the required dlib face recognition models.
.PP
It needs to be started with root privileges, which is handled through
polkit when launched from a desktop environment.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-start-auth-ui
Internal option used by howdy to launch the authentication user
interface. Not intended for manual use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/howdy/config.ini
Howdy configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/howdy/models/
Stored face models.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR howdy (1),
project page:
https://github.com/boltgolt/howdy
